# Declare the pad the drone is standing on, at the moment it first arms.
#
# The drone always starts on a base, and that base is NOT one of the sites it is
# meant to land on. Left to the detector it would eventually be seen from the
# air, land in the map as an ordinary candidate, and cost a full travel +
# confirmation hover to rule out — pure position-estimate drift spent proving
# something already known. Registering it instead is free and certain.
#
# Called once, by hydrone_mission/phase1_mission_node, immediately after the
# first successful arm. pad_map_node claims any existing entry within
# takeoff_base_radius of `position` (a base sighted on the ground before arming
# is the same physical thing) and creates one otherwise.

# Where the drone is standing, in the map frame. Normally straight from
# /mavros/local_position/pose.
geometry_msgs/Point position
---
bool success
string message
# Id of the entry that now carries is_takeoff_base, claimed or newly created.
uint16 id
